DESCRIPTION:Update on 7/10/26 Due to low registration number\, we have dec
 ided to change this to an informal pop-up event which means we will NOT be
  covering the cost of anything. All transportation\, bike rentals\, and ho
 tel/camping will be at your discretion. We believe that many of you still 
 want to show up and ride given your love and passion for mountain biking! 
 Camping/hotel recommendations remain the same. We will leave the orginial 
 program up for ride group and schedules. We will NOT be providing guides a
 nd we remind you to prioritize saftey when you're out riding. Campgrounds 
 will not be provided at this event\, but we have some recommendations belo
 w: For this year’s bikeboom event\, we will not be providing campsites\;
  however\, below are some recommendations that we have gotten from locals
 \; we enc\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/bikeboom-2026\n\nSource: BikeReg
 \n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
